cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Pagewright: a local-first book editor for Markdown"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "Mavengence"
url: "https://github.com/Mavengence/pagewright"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Mavengence/pagewright"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-04-27"
abstract: >
  Pagewright is a local-first web editor for writing books, papers,
  and long-form documents in Markdown. It pairs a CodeMirror editor
  with a true paged A4 preview rendered via paged.js, so authors can
  see page breaks update in real time as they write. Themes are plain
  CSS with optional callout label overrides and chapter-opener
  templates, making the same stylesheet drive both the live preview
  and the final PDF render.
keywords:
  - markdown
  - book editor
  - paged.js
  - paged media
  - publishing
  - typography
  - long-form writing
  - print CSS
